# Switchyard Cursor Agent Rules (Open Agent Hackathon 2026)

Always read and follow `AGENTS.md` before modifying any Data, Build, or Power layer code.

## 1. Layer 01 (DATA - Zetaris)
- Run `python3 scripts/preflight.py` before onboarding or modifying Zetaris tables.
- Send **one complete SQL statement at a time** to `POST {ZETARIS_REST_URL}/sql-editor/sqls/run`. Never batch semicolon-separated statements.
- Include `Authorization: Bearer <ZETARIS_API_KEY>`, `X-Org-ID: 1`, and a fresh `uuid.uuid4()` `X-Request-ID` on every REST request.
- Never print or log credentials from `.env` or `.env.local`.

## 2. Layer 02 (BUILD - Cursor & Meterless Engines)
- Maintain working implementations and conformance tests for all four Meterless Engines (`meterless.ai/engines.html`):
  - `agent/engines/scout_intent.py` (Scout Intent)
  - `agent/engines/world_model.py` (World Model with optimistic concurrency control)
  - `agent/engines/markovian.py` (Markovian bounded `CarryOverState` compression)
  - `agent/engines/h_mem.py` (H-MEM 3-tier persistent memory)
- Verify changes with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.

## 3. Layer 03 (POWER - Meterless Nightshift & NVIDIA Nemotron)
- Route all runtime LLM calls through Meterless Nightshift (`http://127.0.0.1:8088/v1`) with `meterless-app: switchyard-agent` and `meterless-scope: user`.
- Keep the NVIDIA API key inside Nightshift (`Setup -> Providers -> NVIDIA`), never inside Cursor's own model provider settings or committed code.
- Record a `ModelReceipt` (`model_handled_by`, `lane`, `latency_ms`, token counts) for every agent step.
